## Real-World Workflow Exposure

The workflow I was exposed to followed this type of structure:

```text
Business Users / Stakeholders
        ↓
I gather business requirements, KPIs, and reporting needs
        ↓
Jira / Confluence
User stories, acceptance criteria, data mappings, documentation, validation rules
        ↓
Data Engineering Team
I translate business needs into technical/data requirements
        ↓
Source Systems
SAP / on-prem systems / enterprise databases
        ↓
Azure Data Factory Pipeline
Pipeline orchestration and scheduled ingestion
        ↓
Lookup Activity
Reads metadata/control tables to identify what needs to be loaded
        ↓
Copy Activity + SHIR
Copies data from SAP or on-prem systems through Self-Hosted Integration Runtime
        ↓
ADLS Gen2 Bronze Layer
Raw data lands as-is for traceability
        ↓
Databricks Silver Layer
Data is cleaned, standardized, validated, and structured
        ↓
Databricks Gold Layer
Business-ready curated data is prepared
        ↓
Azure SQL / Synapse
Final structured data is made available for downstream use
        ↓
Power BI / Tableau / Reporting
Dashboards, KPI tracking, ad hoc analysis, and business insights
```

This flow represents how business reporting needs move from stakeholder conversations into technical pipeline execution and finally into trusted reporting outputs.

