## Where Python Fits In

Python is useful in this workflow because it can help automate monitoring and validation across pipeline outputs.

In this project, Python is used to simulate how pipeline logs and data quality results can be reviewed before data is trusted for reporting.

Python can help identify:

- Pipeline failures
- Late or delayed refreshes
- SLA breaches
- Long-running jobs
- Zero-record loads
- Source-to-target row count mismatches
- Schema changes
- Missing mandatory fields
- Data quality exceptions
- High-priority reporting risks

The goal is not to replace the pipeline tool. The goal is to use Python as a validation and monitoring layer that helps data teams understand whether pipeline outputs are reliable.

