## Where SQL Fits In

SQL is used heavily for validating whether data is accurate, complete, and ready for reporting.

SQL checks can be used to validate:

- Source-to-target record counts
- Duplicate business keys
- Missing required fields
- Invalid dates
- Bronze vs Silver vs Gold layer differences
- Business rule outputs
- KPI calculation logic
- Reporting layer readiness

Example SQL use cases:

```text
Compare source count vs target count
Check duplicate product/store/date records
Validate that mandatory fields are populated
Confirm that open quantity logic is accurate
Review whether current inventory records loaded correctly
Confirm that sales history covers the expected time period
```

SQL is also used for ad hoc investigation when dashboards show unexpected values or when business users question reporting outputs.

